# Read by live-build's binary_rootfs stage (scripts/build/binary_rootfs
# upstream) as an mksquashfs -ef exclude list (wildcards enabled) when it
# packs chroot/ into filesystem.squashfs - this is live-build's own knob
# for dropping paths from the image, not a dpkg-level exclude, so it
# needs no ordering against when packages install: it only ever applies
# once, at the very end, when the squashfs is written.
#
# Every pattern below is documentation/translation data with no runtime
# role in this image: live-boot, systemd-networkd, kezio-agent, and
# ezio's runtime libraries read none of it. The live OS here is a
# headless, non-interactive deploy agent - nothing in the boot/agent
# path prints a man page, a --help page's own --help text, or a
# translated string, so English-only source strings (gettext's
# untranslated fallback, which every one of these packages already
# carries outside of usr/share/locale) are enough. This is a standard
# live-image slimming step; see the 100-300 MiB filesystem.squashfs
# target this build works against (dist/live/manifest.json, reported by
# .github/workflows/build-live-image.yml).
usr/share/doc/*
usr/share/man/*
usr/share/groff/*
usr/share/info/*
usr/share/lintian/*
usr/share/locale/*
